# Artistry and exceptions

Read [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) → Cabinet undertone.

## Undertone ≠ Easter egg

The cabinet's personality is **continuous** — felt, held pieces, card flip, quiet chrome — not a hidden joke or one-off animation buried in settings.

Players should feel they opened a **physical cabinet on a small screen**, every visit.

## Whimsy with a job

Whimsy must **help** play or recognition:

| Whimsy with a job | Not whimsy |
|---|---|
| Connect Four disc held above the column before drop | Confetti on win in chrome |
| Card flip / deal weight on shared tabletop kit | Random mascot on every empty state |
| Stone piles, meeple snap, dice land | Life-app celebration checkmarks |
| Brand stamp on wordmark | Sparkle / "AI" badges |

One **specific** delight beats generic whimsy pasted on every surface.

## Quiet ordinary makes exceptional visible

Ordinary chrome stays calm so boards, tokens, and motion can carry character. If everything shouts, nothing reads.

## Breaking rules

You may break spacing, colour, or motion rules **only with intention**:

- Name the player moment it serves.
- Keep it local to that game or that interaction — do not fork the whole design system.
- Document in `DESIGN.md` or a game override, not as a new global default.

## Explicit exclusions (this product)

Not a habit/task manager UI. Not Prism-style extension chrome. Not SaaS landing density. Not security-shop alarm red on every control.

Conflicts: favour **intentionality.mdc** and **GamesCabinet undertone** over template polish.
